From a908745a9e725808d1a07500b5104ecc966176f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:40:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 237/239] ipa: rkisp2: Share the ISO step calibration helpers

The Rockchip AIQ calibrates its noise reduction and sharpening per ISO
step and runs them on one gain state, the ratio by which the gain map
is scaled at low and high gain. The temporal noise reduction kept both
the calibration helpers and that state to itself.

Move the helpers to a calibration module and the gain, its ratio and
the use of the gain map to the active state, where the spatial noise
reduction can use them too.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
